      "research_entry": "Finite-volume boundary estimate for auxiliary cube voids in the source-marked tile assembly. Compare equal constituent volumes with the nonoverlapping equal-size cubes. Within a large observation cube only an O(R^2) boundary layer can change the two volume sums. Every repetitive open hole has positive lower volume density, giving grid rigidity for repetitive assemblies. After the grid step, on a finite cyclic fibre the exact marked-voxel multiplicity is 1-b(x)+b(x-w). Determine the optimal distance to invariance and the full attainable defect vs repair profile.",
      "scope": "Different publication and theorem from wave14 two-colour stacking. The external-source paper assumes exact constituent tilings, near-centre rigidity and type separation. Sparse holes or near-kernel bounds alone cannot imply a native or Euclidean no-tiling theorem.",
